<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Amba Sel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1531">1531</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-adal-war">Ethiopian–Adal War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Amba Sel was fought in 1531 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopian-highlands">Ethiopian highlands</a> between the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-ibn-ibrahim-al-ghazi">Imam Ahmad</a> ibn Ibrahim al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi">Ghazi</a> of Adal and the army of the Ethiopian emperor Lebna Dengel. Adal won, continuing its advance into the Christian highlands. It was one of a series of victories that allowed Adal to occupy much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>.</p></div>
